```
So `paths.count == 400` fails `> 400` and takes the single-call branch: exactly 400 paths is ONE invocation, 401 is two (400 + 1). `--literal-pathspecs` is placed BEFORE the `diff` subcommand, i.e. it is a git-level option, appended after the `-c core.quotepath=false -c color.ui=false` pair from Git.run:43.
With `paths: []` (non-nil, empty): `paths == nil` is false so `--literal-pathspecs` IS prepended; the guard's else branch runs; `if let paths` succeeds so `["--"] + []` appends a bare `--`; the command becomes `git -c core.quotepath=false -c color.ui=false --literal-pathspecs diff --no-ext-diff -M <from> <to> --`, which git reads as 'no pathspec' -> a FULL-TREE diff. There is no `guard !paths.isEmpty else { return ... }`, unlike `resetIndex` (Git.swift:388 `guard !paths.isEmpty else { return }`), `checkoutPaths` (:394), `removePaths` (:399), `restore` (:602) and `previewRestore` (:582 `guard !paths.isEmpty else { return RevertPreview(files: []) }`).
