SOURCE FACT on the locations, WRONG on what the second one means. Exactly three call sites repo-wide, all in DiffInspector.swift.
The rule, TouchedPaths.swift:55-59:
```
nonisolated static func matches(_ file: DiffFile, touched: Set<String>) -> Bool {
    [file.path, file.oldPath].compactMap { $0 }.contains { path in
        touched.contains(path) || touched.contains { $0.hasSuffix("/" + path) || path.hasSuffix("/" + $0) }
    }
}
```
Exact match on either `file.path` or `file.oldPath`, else a suffix match in EITHER direction, always with an interposed `/`.
Site 1 -- DiffInspector.swift:143-148, and the critic's description is right:
```
let focus = Set(runtime.diffFocusEdits.map(\.path))
let focused = focus.isEmpty ? [] : files.filter { TouchedPaths.matches($0, touched: focus) }.map(\.id)
if !focused.isEmpty {
    collapsed = Set(files.map(\.id)).subtracting(focused)
    scrollTarget = focused.first
    scrollRequest += 1
} else if files.count > 6, collapsed.isEmpty {
    collapsed = Set(files.dropFirst().map(\.id))
} else {
    collapsed = collapsed.intersection(files.map(\.id))
}
```
So the loose suffix rule decides which diff rows open on arrival and which one the view scrolls to (DiffFile.id is its `path`, DiffParser.swift:19). A false positive opens the wrong file and scrolls to it; a false negative falls through to the `files.count > 6` rule (first file open, rest collapsed).
Sites 2 and 3 -- DiffInspector.swift:162-173, `focusedFiles(_ edits:missingFrom:)`. The critic says 'a turn is skipped when neither files nor missing matches'. THAT IS BACKWARDS AND AT THE WRONG GRANULARITY. The real code:
```
for edit in edits {
    guard !edit.path.isEmpty, let patch = edit.diff, !patch.isEmpty else { continue }
    let touched: Set<String> = [edit.path]
    guard !files.contains(where: { TouchedPaths.matches($0, touched: touched) }),
          !missing.contains(where: { TouchedPaths.matches($0, touched: touched) }) else { continue }
    let file = DiffParser.parseHunks(patch, path: edit.path)
    if !file.hunks.isEmpty { missing.append(file) }
}
```
The loop is over EDITS, not turns. An edit is SKIPPED when a match IS found (in the already-parsed `files` or in the `missing` accumulator) -- i.e. matching means 'already covered, do not synthesize a duplicate'. `touched` is a one-element set holding the edit's own path, so the suffix rule here is a de-duplication key. The result feeds DiffInspector.swift:136-138 `files = missing.isEmpty ? parsed : missing + parsed`.

